; SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
;
; FunctionFlags — the four bits GetFunctionFlags answers with, ported from the
; reference's internal/ast/functionflags.go.
;
; Hand-ported for the reasons NodeFlags.scaly and ModifierFlags.scaly give:
; upstream writes that file by hand, it is four lines, and the composite reads
; better spelled out than derived. The composite stays SYMBOLIC — a module-level
; `define` initializer folds constant identifiers as well as literals — so a
; changed bit position cannot leave a stale composite behind.
;
; ★★ THE COMPOSITE IS TESTED FOR EQUALITY, NOT FOR OVERLAP, and that is the whole
; reason it exists. checkSignatureDeclaration asks `flags & AsyncGenerator ==
; AsyncGenerator` for *this is an async generator* and `flags & AsyncGenerator ==
; Async` for *this is async and NOT a generator* — two questions one mask cannot
; answer with a non-zero test. Reading either as an overlap test is a well-formed
; wrong answer, so the mask is named rather than written out at the three sites.
;
; Upstream declares this uint32. Here it is int (i64); the bit POSITIONS are what
; the reference fixes and nothing crosses a C boundary, so the width is free.

define FunctionFlagsNormal:         int 0
define FunctionFlagsGenerator:      int 1 << 0
define FunctionFlagsAsync:          int 1 << 1
define FunctionFlagsInvalid:        int 1 << 2   ; e.g., invalid !async or !generator
define FunctionFlagsAsyncGenerator: int FunctionFlagsAsync | FunctionFlagsGenerator
